# The vehicle examples' backend-neutral data (docs/physics-two-implementations.md
# §3, docs/physics-design.md §5.7): Box3D's Driving sample as plain Rae data,
# so 124_vehicle_port and 125_vehicle_c build the same car on the same course
# through their own track's ECS layer. No physics track is imported here.
#
# FRAMES. Box3D's sample is Y-up; Rae's world is Z-up (docs/coordinate-
# system.md). The car keeps the sample's numbers in its own Y-up local frame,
# and its bodies are placed with `localToWorld` (a +90 degree turn about x:
# local y becomes world z, local z becomes world -y), so every body-local
# position and joint frame is Box3D's, verbatim. The car drives along its
# local -x, which is world -x.
open Vec3
open Quat
open physicsScenes/SceneTypes

# One wheel: where its joint sits on the chassis (chassis-local, Y-up) and
# what the wheel does.
type VehicleWheel {
  chassisPoint: Vec3
  steers: Bool
  drives: Bool
  # The axle this wheel is on, for the torque split: true at the front
  front: Bool
}

# The car: a box chassis, four sphere wheels on wheel joints (suspension,
# steering, spin motor), the drive (motor speed, total torque and its split
# between the axles), and the keep-upright parallel joint.
type VehicleDescription {
  chassisHalfExtents: Vec3
  chassisDensity: Float
  wheelRadius: Float
  wheelDensity: Float
  wheelFriction: Float
  wheels: List(VehicleWheel)
  # Wheel joint frames: on the chassis (its x axis is the suspension and
  # steering axis) and on the wheel (its z axis is the axle)
  chassisFrameRotation: Quat
  wheelFrameRotation: Quat
  # A wheel body's rotation relative to the chassis
  wheelRotation: Quat
  suspensionHertz: Float
  suspensionDampingRatio: Float
  lowerSuspensionLimit: Float
  upperSuspensionLimit: Float
  steeringHertz: Float
  steeringDampingRatio: Float
  maxSteeringTorque: Float
  lowerSteeringLimit: Float
  upperSteeringLimit: Float
  maxSteeringAngle: Float
  # The spin motors' top speed (radians per second) and total torque, split
  # `rearDriveShare` to the rear axle and the rest to the front
  spinSpeed: Float
  totalSpinTorque: Float
  rearDriveShare: Float
  # Keep upright: the chassis frame held parallel to the venue's
  uprightFrameRotation: Quat
  uprightHertz: Float
  uprightDampingRatio: Float
  # World pose of the chassis at spawn
  startPosition: Vec3
  localToWorld: Quat
}

# The driver's input: throttle forward (+1) to reverse (-1), steering left
# (+1) to right (-1).
type VehicleCommand {
  throttle: Float
  steer: Float
}

# What the adapter sets on one wheel joint this frame.
type VehicleWheelTarget {
  steeringAngle: Float
  spinSpeed: Float
  maxSpinTorque: Float
}

# The course: a height-field terrain (Box3D's grid over local x and z with
# heights along local y, placed by `terrainPosition` / `terrainRotation`),
# static ramps and walls, and crates to knock over (respawned with the car).
type VehicleCourse {
  heights: List(Float)
  countX: Int
  countZ: Int
  terrainScale: Vec3
  terrainPosition: Vec3
  terrainRotation: Quat
  terrainFriction: Float
  fixtures: List(SceneBody)
  crates: List(SceneBody)
  cameraStart: Vec3
}
